+    "exported_at": "2026-08-30T14:41:26Z",
+    "body_digest": "sha256:067561fa0656fbb4de902f42bde53eb0f0df1964aa35ed550845ce428db4854c"
+  },
+  "title": "GOV-0081: WP-BLD-B — G07 evidence schemas (source-change/build/unit-test/documentation) + self-dossier extension + build ledger; badf-build → IMPLEMENTED",
+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-2)** — plan for WP-BLD-B: G07 evidence schemas + self-dossier extension + build ledger (`badf-build` → `IMPLEMENTED`)\n\n## Stage-Gate\n- **Stage:** 4 prototype → the first executable substrate of the frozen contract, on BADF's own Work Packages.\n- **Decision:** Continue — rung B of the operator-authorized ladder (#188).\n- **Over-engineering risk:** a second producer of G07 evidence, or a `scripts/badf_build.py`. Refused (BLD-I18): the canonical producer is `badf_gate.py self-dossier` and this WP **extends** it; schemas specialize the existing `evidence.schema.json`, they do not replace it.\n- **Glossary stage(s):** 7 build; G08 untouched.\n\n## Observed (the gap, measured on `main`)\n`self_dossier()` already emits the four G07 objects for every BADF WP, but as weak instances: `source_revision: \"HEAD\"` (not an exact SHA — violates BLD-I16), `unit-test` is `NOT_RUN` / `deferred-to-compose` with a placeholder artifact (no red/green, counts or command — BLD-I07/I09 have no evidence object), `source-change` binds a diff digest but **no base/head SHA pair, no changed-path list, no expected-surface comparison** (BLD-I04 has nothing to judge), `build` is `py_compile` with `toolchain.version: \"1\"` (no environment identity), `documentation` answers \"what docs changed\" but not \"what was NOT updated and why\". No `schemas/{source-change,build,unit-test,documentation}.schema.json` exist. No build ledger exists.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (WP-2026-0098 / BADF-DEM-0085)\n- **Four schemas** `schemas/source-change.schema.json`, `build.schema.json`, `unit-test.schema.json`, `documentation.schema.json` — each a *specialization* of `evidence.schema.json` (same required core; `evidence_type` const; a typed `binding` object carrying the G07 contract fields from `references/g07-contract.md`: source-change → `base_sha`, `head_sha`, `changed_paths`, `change_digest`, `expected_surfaces`, `unexpected_paths`; build → `command`, `cwd`, `environment` (python/os identity), `exit_code`, `artifacts[{ref,digest}]`, `non_coverage`; unit-test → `obligations[{id, acceptance_ref, seam, red{observed,ref}, green{observed,ref}}]`, `command`, `result`, `tests_run`, `failures`, `coverage_scope`; documentation → `changed`, `contract_changed`, `behavior_changed`, `required_updates`, `not_updated_with_reason`). Additive: existing generic objects on `main` stay valid under `evidence.schema.json`; the typed schema binds only objects that declare `binding`.\n- **`self_dossier` extension (the canonical producer, BLD-I18):** binds exact `base_sha`/`head_sha` and `changed_paths`; computes the **expected-surface comparison** from the WP's optional `expected_surfaces` (WP-IMP-B field) — absent → declared `non_coverage`, present → `unexpected_paths` listed and the dossier `HELD` with reason when non-empty (BLD-I04, at packaging time); `build` records python/OS identity; `unit-test` binds the WP's `tests` modules and an author-supplied run log (`evidence/G07/unit-test.txt`) parsed for `Ran N tests … OK|FAILED` with the log's digest, `outcome` from the parse, and the composed-tree gate named as the fresh authoritative run (BLD-I09) — never `NOT_RUN` when a log is present; `documentation` gains `not_updated_with_reason` from the WP record's `documentation` note or declared non-coverage.\n- **`validate_evidence`** applies the typed schema when `binding` is present (`check_schema(<type>)`), so a malformed binding fails the dossier; generic objects unaffected.\n- **Build ledger** `work/<WP>/build/{session.json, progress.jsonl, decisions.jsonl}` — schema `schemas/build-ledger-event.schema.json` (or reuse of `run-ledger-event.schema.json` if its contract fits — decided at plan time by inspection, stated in the PR); `self-dossier` appends `START/BASELINE/VERIFY/HANDOFF` events for its own run; the ledger is recovery/evidence, never authority (no gate reads it for a verdict).\n- **Registry:** `badf-build` `DESIGNED → IMPLEMENTED`, digest re-pinned only if `SKILL.md` changes (it should not).\n- **No** `scripts/badf_build.py`; no lifecycle change; `content_tree`/composition record semantics unchanged (the ledger lives under `work/<WP>/`, already excluded).\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_badf_build_evidence.py`, failing-first)\n- `test_four_schemas_specialize_evidence_schema` — required core ⊇ evidence.schema required; `evidence_type` const per file.\n- `test_self_dossier_binds_exact_shas_and_changed_paths` — scratch WP: `base_sha`/`head_sha` are 40-hex and equal `git rev-parse`; `changed_paths` equals `git diff --name-only` minus `work/<WP>/` and the lockfile.\n- `test_expected_surface_comparison` — WP with `expected_surfaces` and one out-of-surface path → `unexpected_paths` non-empty and dossier `HELD` with the BLD-I04 reason; without `expected_surfaces` → `non_coverage` declared.\n- `test_unit_test_binding_parses_run_log` — log `Ran 12 tests … OK` → `tests_run 12`, `outcome PASS`, digest bound; `FAILED (failures=1)` → `outcome FAIL`; absent log → `NOT_RUN` with reason.\n- `test_build_records_environment_identity`; `test_documentation_not_updated_with_reason`.\n- `test_typed_binding_is_validated` — a malformed `binding` fails `dossier` with the schema's message; a generic object still passes.\n- `test_ledger_events_are_appended_and_never_read_for_verdict`.\n- Existing `test_badf_self_dossier` / `test_badf_reconcile` / composition & integration fixtures stay green (they carry `work/` and `schemas/`).\n- Mutation: each new control's refusal disabled one at a time → its test red.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Deterministic controls beyond packaging-time surface comparison (authority-before-mutation, red-before-green enforcement, budget/stop, delegation subset) — **BLD-C**. Shadow — BLD-D. Admission — BLD-E.\n- Running the unit tests inside `self-dossier` (the composed-tree gate is the fresh run; the self-dossier binds the author's log and the gate's result).\n\n**Version tier:** minor (new schemas + producer extension, backward-compatible). **Lean mode:** enforced (schemas additive; no new tool). QA + REV: BARCHI-1 (shared surface).\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n",
+  "authorized_by": {
+    "principal": "operator",
+    "principal_type": "human"
+  },
+  "recorded_at": "2026-08-30T14:41:26Z",
+  "provenance": "EXPORTED_FROM_SOURCE",
+  "status": "AUTHORIZED",
+  "note": "WP-BLD-B: four typed G07 evidence schemas (source-change/build/unit-test/documentation) specializing evidence.schema.json; self_dossier extended to bind exact base/head SHAs + content tree + changed paths + expected-surface comparison (BLD-I04/I16), the author's unit-test log (BLD-I07/I09), build environment identity and documentation non-update reasons; typed bindings validated at production and on the dossier; hash-chained build ledger (run-ledger-event records) never read for a verdict. badf-build DESIGNED -> IMPLEMENTED."
+}
